WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:02.368
- Hey guys, I'm Yara, I'm from Grown-ish

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:04.919
and today I will be reading
some college horror stories.

00:00:04.919 --> 00:00:08.086
(spooky upbeat music)

00:00:11.018 --> 00:00:12.685
So, let's get to it.

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:33.280
- Okay, my question is did
she actually spill milk

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.280
or was she imagining it?

00:00:37.493 --> 00:00:39.555
I wonder how the rest
of the year went though?

00:00:39.555 --> 00:00:42.894
I want to know, if this was
only a couple nights in,

00:00:42.894 --> 00:00:45.144
do you just get used to it?

00:01:10.454 --> 00:01:12.363
You know, I wouldn't
be mad at that though.

00:01:12.363 --> 00:01:14.822
My major plan is that
once I get my degree,

00:01:14.822 --> 00:01:15.682
I'm going to create a school

00:01:15.682 --> 00:01:19.502
and the only class they'll
teach is called AP Common Sense

00:01:19.502 --> 00:01:22.272
and the major skill that
they will be teaching

00:01:22.272 --> 00:01:24.262
is how to file taxes.

00:01:24.262 --> 00:01:26.571
And you know, I kind of
want to sign this girl up

00:01:26.571 --> 00:01:27.752
to teach a class.

00:01:27.752 --> 00:01:29.603
It just makes me wonder,

00:01:29.603 --> 00:01:32.022
what was she doing
beforehand that inspired her

00:01:32.022 --> 00:01:36.022
to go into somebody's
room and file their taxes?

00:01:49.122 --> 00:01:53.003
Okay, I don't know how
to respond to that one.

00:01:53.003 --> 00:01:56.822
It's almost, how did
they get the goat inside?

00:01:56.822 --> 00:02:00.872
How did the goat get into
the dorm in the first place.

00:02:00.872 --> 00:02:04.289
It's a lot of creative people in college.

00:02:17.152 --> 00:02:19.290
How considerate.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.320
That's amazing, I mean,

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:24.622
the thing is, I've never
stored a rat in our fridge

00:02:24.622 --> 00:02:27.712
but I am infamous for having
little experiments that I do

00:02:27.712 --> 00:02:30.352
because I used to just use all that really

00:02:30.352 --> 00:02:32.232
organic expensive food and like,

00:02:32.232 --> 00:02:33.571
I'm going to mix it all together

00:02:33.571 --> 00:02:36.262
and I'm going to do some
chemical reaction with it.

00:02:36.262 --> 00:02:37.952
There are plenty of times of
having to tell my brothers

00:02:37.952 --> 00:02:40.289
that that wasn't food and not to eat it.

00:02:40.289 --> 00:02:42.372
So, I can kind of relate.

00:02:53.911 --> 00:02:56.371
Squirrels don't like me.

00:02:56.371 --> 00:02:58.942
There was a squirrel at my high school

00:02:58.942 --> 00:03:00.663
and I had this one long walk.

00:03:00.663 --> 00:03:03.122
It would literally just
follow me the entire time

00:03:03.122 --> 00:03:05.122
but it was as though
it was waiting for me.

00:03:05.122 --> 00:03:06.602
I would see it as soon
as I opened the door,

00:03:06.602 --> 00:03:07.962
it would just be sitting there

00:03:07.962 --> 00:03:10.932
and I had to try and
get into my class safely

00:03:10.932 --> 00:03:12.742
without being attacked by a squirrel.

00:03:12.742 --> 00:03:14.181
It was fun times.

00:03:14.181 --> 00:03:16.764
(upbeat music)

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:21.615
Thanks for watching guys.

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:25.869
(upbeat music)

